## ARCHITECTURE

Monorepo structure inside "oorjaman-flagship":

- apps/
  - customer-app (Expo + Expo Router)
  - technician-app (Expo + Expo Router)
  - admin-web (React Vite - OorjaMan operations staff)
  - vendor-web (React Vite - vendor partner portal)

- packages/
  - ui (cross-platform components)
  - config (theme, fonts, spacing)
  - api (supabase client + queries)
  - utils (hooks/helpers)

- supabase/
  - schema.sql
  - policies.sql

---

## EXPO RULES (MANDATORY)

- Use Expo Router (NOT React Navigation manually)

- Use file-based routing inside app/ directory

- Use expo-font for fonts

- Use expo-splash-screen for splash handling

- Use expo-secure-store for tokens

- Use expo-image for optimized images

- Use expo-location for GPS

- Follow latest Expo patterns only

- Avoid deprecated APIs

---

## UI / UX RULES (MODERN 2025)

- Clean, minimal, premium UI
- Smooth animations (use Reanimated if needed)
- Skeleton loaders (no blocking spinners)
- Bottom tabs for primary navigation
- Gesture-friendly interactions
- Proper empty states

ONBOARDING FLOW:

- Splash screen (brand logo)
- 2-3 onboarding slides (value props)
- Permission screens (location, notifications)
- OTP login

AUTH UX:

- Mobile-first OTP login
- Auto-fill OTP where possible
- Persistent login session

PERFORMANCE:

- Lazy load screens
- Use FlashList for lists
- Avoid re-renders
- Optimistic updates

TECHNICIAN UX:

- Extremely simple UI
- Big buttons
- Minimal steps
- Offline-safe interactions

---

## STATE & DATA

- React Query (server state)
- Zustand (client state)
- Supabase client from packages/api

---

## BUSINESS RULES

VENDOR:

- Vendors must be approved before visibility

BOOKING:

- Customer selects vendor + slot
- Vendor accepts within 1 hour
- Booking code is generated

TECHNICIAN FLOW:

- Booking code required
- Safety checklist mandatory
- Timer-based execution
- Before/after photos required

AMC / SUBSCRIPTIONS:

- Recurring cleaning plans
- Monthly / Quarterly frequencies
- Auto-generate bookings
- Pause / Resume / Cancel

---

## CODE QUALITY

- TypeScript strict mode
- Reusable components
- Modular structure
- No inline styles
- Theme-based styling only

---

## ALWAYS FOLLOW

- Use Expo Router for navigation
- Use shared components from packages/ui
- Use theme from packages/config
- Use API layer from packages/api
- Keep everything production-ready
